y" type="B"><help>Flag indicating that the values in this field are read-only. This applied to the UI-level editing and some data model level operations as well.</help><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field><field description="Nullable" name="nullable" type="B"><help>Flag indicating that field can contain NULL values.</help><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field><field description="Key" name="key" type="B"><help>Flag indicating that the field is a part of record’s unique ID, which is a unique combination of all key fields defined in the table format. Any declared key fields usually force the Data Table Smart Copy operation to employ a special copy algorithm that match records by their unique key field combinations rather than record numbers.</help><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field><field description="Selection Values" name="selvals" type="T"><help>List of values that can be selected for the field via a drop-down menu. A description must be defined for each value. Descriptions are shown when displaying the table to a user, and the values are available when the cell is referenced inside the platform.</help><defaultValue><table><format reorderable="true"><fields><field description="Value" keyfield="true" name="value" nullable="true" type="S"><defaultValue><nullValue/></defaultValue></field><field description="Description" name="description" type="S"><defaultValue/></field></fields><validators contentType="base64">HEseHQ==</validators></format></table></defaultValue></field><field description="Extendable Selection Values" name="extselvals" type="B"><help>Flag indicating the field may be set to any value, including ones not listed in Selection Values.</help><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field><field advanced="true" description="Hidden" name="hidden" type="B"><help>The setting hides the field in the UI, but it remains accessible at the data model level.</help><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field><field advanced="true" description="Inline" name="inline" type="B"><help>&lt;p>This flag has special meaning for different fields:&lt;/p>&lt;ul>&lt;li>If the Inline flag is set for a Data Block field, the field value will be stored in a dedicated database table. The value will not be initially loaded if the table itself is loaded from the database and sent to a IoT Platform Client or external application. The Data Block value will, however, contain a data block ID that can be used to force loading the Data Block data from the server database. This is suitable for large binary values, such as image, sound, and video files.&lt;/li>&lt;li>If Inline flag is set for a Color field, field value will be used to highlight records of the table when its being viewed/edited in a Data Table Editor. Its often feasible to combine Inline flag with a Hidden flag to hide the Color field itself from the table. See the Row Coloring section below for more information.&lt;/li>&lt;li>If Inline flag is set for a Data Table field, default value of the field will have same format as format of the table to which the field belongs. This effectively enables creation of tables with unlimited nesting using Data Table Editor.&lt;/li>&lt;/ul></help><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field><field advanced="true" description="Encrypted" name="encrypted" type="B"><help>Enables database-level field value encryption.</help><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field><field description="Help" editor="textarea" name="help" nullable="true" type="S"><validators contentType="base64">HFIeW15ccHtDbnRybH1dKl5eRGVzY3JpcHRpb24gbWF5IGNvbnRhaW4gb25seSBwcmludGFibGUgY2hhcmFjdGVycx0=</validators><help>Contents of the pop-up which is displayed to the user when hovering over a field.</help><defaultValue><nullValue/></defaultValue></field><field description="Editor/Viewer" extendableSelectionValues="true" name="editor" nullable="true" type="S"><selectionValues><option description="Default"><nullValue/></option><option description="List">list</option><option description="Date">date</option><option des