option><option description="Right">right</option></selectionValues><defaultValue><nullValue/></defaultValue></field><field description="Border Top" name="borderTop" type="S"><defaultValue/></field><field description="Border Left" name="borderLeft" type="S"><defaultValue/></field><field description="Border Right" name="borderRight" type="S"><defaultValue/></field><field description="Border Bottom" name="borderBottom" type="S"><defaultValue/></field><field description="Text Transfer" name="textTransfer" type="S"><defaultValue>trim</defaultValue></field><field description="Custom Classes" name="customCssClasses" type="S"><defaultValue/></field></fields></format><records><record/></records></table></defaultValue></field></fields></format><records><record/></records></table></defaultValue></field><field description="Formats" name="formats" type="T"><defaultValue><table><format><fields><field description="ID" keyfield="true" name="id" type="L"><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field><field description="Format" name="format" type="S"><defaultValue/></field></fields></format><records><record><value name="format">&lt;&gt;&lt;S>&lt;F=NR>&lt;A=&lt;NULL>>&lt;E=textarea></value></record></records></table></defaultValue></field><field description="Highest Row Index" name="highestRowIndex" type="I"><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field><field description="Highest Column Index" name="highestColumnIndex" type="I"><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field></fields></format><records><record/></records></table></defaultValue></field></fields><validators contentType="base64">HEseHQ==</validators></format></entry><entry><int>11</int><format><fields><field description="Channel Name" keyfield="true" name="name" nullable="true" type="S"><validators contentType="base64">HEweMSAyMTQ3NDgzNjQ3HRxSHlx3K15eTmFtZSBtYXkgY29udGFpbiBvbmx5IExhdGluIGxldHRlcnMsIGRpZ2l0cywgYW5kIHVuZGVyc2NvcmVzHQ==</validators><help>This is a unique channel ID used to refer to channel data.</help><defaultValue><nullValue/></defaultValue></field><field description="Variable" extendableSelectionValues="true" icon="fi_variable" name="variable" type="S"><help>Name of the variable whose value will be used in the statistical channel.</help><defaultValue/></field><field description="Enabled" name="enabled" type="B"><help>Controls whether the channel is active and collects data. Default channels should be disabled instead of deleting them in order to prevent their recreation.</help><defaultValue>1</defaultValue></field><field description="Parameters" icon="var_statistics" name="parameters" nullable="true" type="T"><help>These are parameters of statistical data collection, storage and processing.</help><defaultValue><table><format maxRecords="1" minRecords="1"><fields><field description="Expression" editor="expression" name="expression" type="S"><help>The &lt;b>Expression&lt;/b> property defines what data is the base of statistics. It is evaluated on every change of variable that the channel is built upon.The expression must evaluate to a number (integer of floating point). If the expression evaluates to any other data type, the system tries to convert it to a number and skips the value if conversion fails. If the expression evaluates to NULL, the system applies &lt;b>NULL Value Handling&lt;/b> method to it.</help><defaultValue/></field><field description="Average" name="average" type="B"><help>This function calculates an average of Primary Data Points to form a Consolidated Data Point. This is an average of values themselves (for &lt;a href="doc://ls_internals_statistics_channel_types">Gauge&lt;/a> channel) or value change rates (for &lt;a href="doc://ls_internals_statistics_channel_types">Counter&lt;/a> and other channel types).</help><group>Aggregation</group><defaultValue>1</defaultValue></field><field description="Minimum" name="minimum" type="B"><help>This function takes finds the minimal Primary Data Point to use as a Consolidated Data Point. This is minimal value itself (for &lt;a href="doc://ls_internals_statistics_channel_types">Gauge&lt;/a> channel) or minimal value change rate (for &lt;a href="doc://ls_internals_statistics_channel_types">Counter&lt;/a> and other channel types).</help><group>Aggregation</group><defaultValue>1</defaultValue></field><field description="Maximum" name="maximum" type="B"><help>Similar to &lt;b>Minimum&lt;/b>.</help><group>Aggregation</group><defaultValue>1</defaultValue></field><field description="Total" name="total" type="B"><help>This function sums all Primary Data Points to form a Consolidated Data Point. This is a sum of values themselves (for &lt;a href="doc://ls_internals_statistics_channel_types">Gauge&lt;/a> channel) or value change rates (for &lt;a href="doc://ls_internals_statistics_channel_types">Counter&lt;/a> and other channel types).</help><group>Aggregation</group><defaultValue>1</defaultValue></field><field description="First" name="first" type="B"><help>This function takes first Primary Data Point as the value for a Consolidated Data Point.</help><group>Aggregation</group><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field><field description="Last" name="last" type="B"><help>This function takes last Primary Data Point as the value for a Consolidated Data Point.</help><group>Aggregation</group><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field><field description="Minutely" editor="period" name="minutelyStats" nullable="true" type="L"><editorOptions>2 3</editorOptions><validators contentType="base64">HEweMTIwMDAwIDkyMjMzNzIwMzY4NTQ3NzU4MDcd</validators><help>Storage period for minutely aggregates.</help><group>Storage Periods</group><defaultValue>3600000</defaultValue></field><field description="Hourly" editor="period" name="hourlyStats" nullable="true" type="L"><editorOptions>3 4</editorOptions><validators contentType="base64">HEweNzIwMDAwMCA5MjIzMzcyMDM2ODU0Nzc1ODA3HQ==</validators><help>Storage period for hourly aggregates.</help><group>Storage Periods</group><defaultValue>86400000</defaultValue></field><field description="Daily" editor="period" name="dailyStats" nullable="true" type="L"><editorOptions>4 6</editorOptions><validators contentType="base64">HEweMTcyODAwMDAwIDkyMjMzNzIwMzY4NTQ3NzU4MDcd</validators><help>Storage period for daily aggregates.</help><group>Storage Periods</group><defaultValue>2592000000</defaultValue></field><field description="Weekly" editor="period" name="weeklyStats" nullable="true" type="L"><editorOptions>5 8</editorOptions><validators contentType="base64">HEweMTIwOTYwMDAwMCA5MjIzMzcyMDM2ODU0Nzc1ODA3HQ==</validators><help>Storage period for weekly aggregates.</help><group>Storage Periods</group><defaultValue>7776000000</defaultValue></field><field description="Monthly" editor="period" name="monthlyStats" nullable="true" type="L"><editorOptions>6 8</editorOptions><validators contentType="base64">HEweNTE4NDAwMDAwMCA5MjIzMzcyMDM2ODU0Nzc1ODA3HQ==</validators><help>Storage period for monthly aggregates.</help><group>Storage Periods</group><defaultValue>31536000000</defaultValue></field><field description="Yearly" editor="period" name="yearlyStats" nullable="true" type="L"><editorOptions>8 8</editorOptions><validators contentType="base64">HEweNjMwNzIwMDAwMDAgOTIyMzM3MjAzNjg1NDc3NTgwNx0=</validators><help>Storage period for yearly aggregates.</help><group>Storage Periods</group><defaultValue>315360000000</defaultValue></field><field description="Timestamp Expression" editor="expression" name="timestampExpression" nullable="true" type="S"><help>Use this expression to override a default timestamp for each new variable value. The expression should evaluate to Date type.</help><group>Advanced Properties</group><defaultValue>{#timestamp}</defaultValue></field><field description="Use Key Field" name="useKeyField" type="B"><help>If Use Key Field is disabled (the default setting), a single Dataset (i.e. set of statistical data) is created for this channel. If Use Key Field is enabled, one Dataset is created for every record in the source variable's value. Enabling this option has sense only for channels based on tabular variables. The name of dataset is defined by the unique record key constructed according to Key Field property.</help><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field><field description="Key Field" name="keyField" nullable="true" type="S"><help>Autodetect if value is NULL</help><defaultValue><nullValue/></defaultValue></field><field description="NULL Value Processing" name="nullValuesProcessing" type="I"><selectionValues><option description="Discard">1</option><option description="Treat As Zero">2</option></selectionValues><help>&lt;p>This setting defines that should the channel do when its &lt;b>Expression&lt;/b> was evaluated to NULL. There are two options:&lt;/p> &lt;ul>&lt;li>&lt;b>Discard&lt;/b>. Value will be silently dropped. If no other values were received for a certain period, channel overall value becomes UNDEFINED for this period.&lt;/li>&lt;li>&lt;b>Treat As Zero&lt;/b>. NULL values will be converted to zeros.&lt;/li>&lt;/ul></help><defaultValue>1</defaultValue></field><field description="Out Of Range Value Processing" name="outOfRangeValuesHandling" type="I"><selectionValues><option description="Do Nothing">0</option><option description="Discard">1</option><option description="Normalize">3</option></selectionValues><help>&lt;p>Specifies how to process the values that are less than &lt;b>Minimum Value&lt;/b> or greater than &lt;b>Maximum Value&lt;/b>. The following choices are available:&lt;/p>&lt;ul>&lt;li>&lt;b>Do Nothing&lt;/b>. Simply disables minimum/maximum values for the channel.&lt;/li>&lt;li>&lt;b>Discard&lt;b>. Drops values that are less than minimum or greater than maximum. If no other values were received for a certain period, channel overall value becomes UNDEFINED for this period.&lt;/li>&lt;li>&lt;b>Normalize&lt;b>. Values less than minimum and greater than maximum are converted to the minimum and maximum values respectively.&lt;/li>&lt;/ul></help><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field><field description="Minimum Value" name="minValue" type="E"><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field><field description="Maximum Value" name="maxValue" type="E"><defaultValue>1</defaultValue></field><field description="Storage" name="storage" type="I"><selectionValues><option description="Standard file (Low memory usage, slow)">0</option><option description="Mapped file (High memory usage, fast)">1</option><option description="Memory (Non-persistent)">2</option><option description="NoSQL Storage">3</option></selectionValues><help>&lt;p>Storage property defines statistics storage type. There are several options:&lt;/p>&lt;ul>&lt;li>Mapped file (Higher memory usage, faster) - the default setting.&lt;/li>&lt;li>Standard file (Lower memory usage, slower).&lt;/li>&lt;li>Memory. Memory based storage guarantees maximum performance, but it doesn't preserve data between server restarts and, therefore, has very limited uses.&lt;/li>&lt;li>NoSQL Storage. Leverages database-level failover, but is much slower compared to file storage.&lt;/li>&lt;/ul></help><defaultValue>1</defaultValue></field><field description="Type" name="type" type="S"><selectionValues><option description="Gauge">GAUGE</option><option description="Counter">COUNTER</option><option description="Derive">DERIVE</option><option description="Absolute">ABSOLUTE</option></selectionValues><help>The channel &lt;b>Type&lt;/b> setting defines how are subsequent source values processed to form &lt;a href="doc://ls_internals_statistics_rrd">Primary Data&lt;/a> Points for the channel.</help><defaultValue>GAUGE</defaultValue></field><field description="Protect Statistics" name="protectStatistics" type="B"><help>Disable parameters that change resets statistics data</help><group>Advanced Properties</group><defaultValue>1</defaultValue></field><field description="Step" editor="period" name="step" type="L"><editorOptions>1 1</editorOptions><validators contentType="base64">HEweMSA5MjIzMzcyMDM2ODU0Nzc1ODA3HQ==</validators><help>Changing this value resets statistics data</help><group>Advanced Properties</group><defaultValue>60000</defaultValue></field><field description="XFiles Factor" name="xff" type="F"><validators contentType="base64">HEweMC4wIDAuOTk5HQ==</validators><help>Changing this value resets statistics data</help><group>Advanced Properties</group><defaultValue>0.9</defaultValue></field><field description="Heartbeat" editor="period" name="heartbeat" type="L"><validators contentType="base64">HEweMCA5MjIzMzcyMDM2ODU0Nzc1ODA3HQ==</validators><help>The maximum time period that may pass between two updates of this data source before the value of the data source is assumed to be 'unknown'. '0' means automatic heartbeat.</help><group>Advanced Properties</group><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field><field description="Data Life Span for Missing Keys" editor="period" name="missedKeysLifespan" type="L"><validators contentType="base64">HEweMCA5MjIzMzcyMDM2ODU0Nzc1ODA3HQ==</validators><help>Time period for that a data archive for a missing key will be stored. If the key is missing for a period shorter than that and then reappear, its associated data will survive. Zero value means removing data just once the the key is disappeared</help><group>Advanced Properties</group><defaultValue>1209600000</defaultValue></field></fields><bindings><binding><reference>keyField#hidden</reference><expression>!{useKeyField}</expression></binding><binding><reference>minValue#hidden</reference><expression>{outOfRangeValuesHandling} == 0</expression></binding><binding><reference>maxValue#hidden</reference><expression>{outOfRangeValuesHandling} == 0</expression></binding><binding><reference>step#enabled</reference><expression>!{protectStatistics}</expression></binding><binding><reference>xff#enabled</reference><expression>!{protectStatistics}</expression></binding><binding><reference>expression#options</reference><expression>hasResolver('parent') ? ({.:childInfo$type[0]} != 1 &amp;&amp; !variableAvailable({.:},{parent/variable}) ? cell(callFunction({.:}, 'expressionEditorOptions',{.:}, {parent/variable})):expressionEditorOptions({.:}, {parent/variable}, 1)): null</expression></binding></bindings><validators contentType="base64">HEUeZTIxcGJsWmhiSFZsZlNBOElIdHRZWGhXWVd4MVpYMGdQeUJ1ZFd4c0lEb2dKMDFwYm1sdGRXMGdWbUZzZFdVZ2MyaHZkV3hrSUdKbElHeGxjM05sY2lCMGFHRnVJRTFoZUdsdGRXMGdWbUZzZFdVbh0=</validators></format><records><record><value name="timestampExpression"><nullValue/></value></record></records></table></defaultValue></field><field description="Inherited From" editor="context" name="inheritedFrom" nullable="true" readonly="true" type="S"><editorOptions contentType="base64"></editorOptions><help>The model that the entity inherits.</help><defaultValue><nullValue/></defaultValue></field></fields><bindings><binding><reference>variable#choices</reference><expression>callFunction({.:}, 'variablesByMask',{.:})</expression></binding></bindings><validators contentType="base64">HEseHQ==</validators></format></entry><entry><int>12</int><format><fields><field description="Name" keyfield="true" name="name" nullable="true" type="S"><validators contentType="base64">HEweMSAyMTQ3NDgzNjQ3HRxSHlx3K15eTmFtZSBtYXkgY29udGFpbiBvbmx5IExhdGluIGxldHRlcnMsIGRpZ2l0cywgYW5kIHVuZGVyc2NvcmVzHQ==</validators><help>A string that identifies the granulator in the context where it is defined.</help><defaultValue><nullValue/></defaultValue></field><field description="Variable" extendableSelectionValues="true" icon="fi_variable" name="variable" type="S"><help>The name of the variable in the context that triggers the granulator.</help><defaultValue/></field><field description="Enabled" name="enabled" type="B"><help>A boolean flag indicating whether the granulator is active and processing variable changes.</help><defaultValue>1</defaultValue></field><field description="Granule Value Format" name="granuleValueFormat" type="T"><help>A format for the table that stores aggregated values.</help><defaultValue><table><format maxRecords="1" minRecords="1" namingExpression="print({fields}, '{name}', ', ')"><fields><field description="Minimal Record Count" name="minRecords" type="I"><validators contentType="base64">HEweMCAyMTQ3NDgzNjQ3HQ==</validators><help>The number of records should be within this range, otherwise the table will be treated as &lt;i>invalid&lt;/i>.</help><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field><field description="Maximal Record Count" extendableSelectionValues="true" name="maxRecords" type="I"><validators contentType="base64">HEweMCAyMTQ3NDgzNjQ3HQ==</validators><selectionValues><option description="Not limited">2147483647</option></selectionValues><help>The number of records should be within this range, otherwise the table will be treated as &lt;i>invalid&lt;/i>.</help><defaultValue>2147483647</defaultValue></field><field description="Fields" name="fields" type="T"><help>Each row in this property defines a field of the data table.</help><defaultValue><table><format reorderable="true"><fields><field hidden="true" name="oldname" type="S"><defaultValue/></field><field description="Name" keyfield="true" name="name" type="S"><validators contentType="base64">HFIeXHcrXl5OYW1lIG1heSBjb250YWluIG9ubHkgTGF0aW4gbGV0dGVycywgZGlnaXRzLCBhbmQgdW5kZXJzY29yZXMd</validators><help>Name of the field. The name is used to refer the field.</help><defaultValue/></field><field description="Type" name="type" type="S"><selectionValues><option description="Data Block">A</option><option description="Boolean">B</option><option description="String">S</option><option description="Color">C</option><option description="Date">D</option><option description="Data Table">T</option><option description="Double">E</option><option description="Float">F</option><option description="Integer">I</option><option description="Long">L</option></selectionValues><help>Type of the field.</help><defaultValue>I</defaultValue></field><field description="Description" name="description" nullable="true" type="S"><validators contentType="base64">HFIeW15ccHtDbnRybH1dKl5eRGVzY3JpcHRpb24gbWF5IGNvbnRhaW4gb25seSBwcmludGFibGUgY2hhcmFjdGVycx0=</validators><help>Textual field description.</help><defaultValue><nullValue/></defaultValue></field><field description="Default" name="defaultValue" nullable="true" type="S"><help>Default value of the field. You can omit this only if the field is nullable.</help><defaultValue><nullValue/></defaultValue></field><field description="Read-only" name="readonly" type="B"><help>Flag indicating that the values in this field are read-only. This applied to the UI-level editing and some data model level operations as well.</help><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field><field description="Nullable" name="nullable" type="B"><help>Flag indicating that field can contain NULL values.</help><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field><field description="Key" name="key" type="B"><help>Flag indicating that the field is a part of record’s unique ID, which is a unique combination of all key fields defined in the table format. Any declared key fields usually force the Data Table Smart Copy operation to employ a special copy algorithm that match records by their unique key field combinations rather than record numbers.</help><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field><field description="Selection Values" name="selvals" type="T"><help>List of values that can be selected for the field via a drop-down menu. A description must be defined for each value. Descriptions are shown when displaying the table to a user, and the values are available when the cell is referenced inside the platform.</help><defaultValue><table><format reorderable="true"><fields><field description="Value" keyfield="true" name="value" nullable="true" type="S"><defaultValue><nullValue/></defaultValue></field><field description="Description" name="description" type="S"><defaultValue/></field></fields><validators contentType="base64">HEseHQ==</validators></format></table></defaultValue></field><field description="Extendable Selection Values" name="extselvals" type="B"><help>Flag indicating the field may be set to any value, including ones not listed in Selection Values.</help><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field><field advanced="true" description="Hidden" name="hidden" type="B"><help>The setting hides the field in the UI, but it remains accessible at the data model level.</help><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field><field advanced="true" description="Inline" name="inline" type="B"><help>&lt;p>This flag has special meaning for different fields:&lt;/p>&lt;ul>&lt;li>If the Inline flag is set for a Data Block field, the field value will be stored in a dedicated database table. The value will not be initially loaded if the table itself is loaded from the database and sent to a IoT Platform Client or external application. The Data Block value will, however, contain a data block ID that can be used to force loading the Data Block data from the server database. This is suitable for large binary values, such as image, sound, and video files.&lt;/li>&lt;li>If Inline flag is set for a Color field, field value will be used to highlight records of the table when its being viewed/edited in a Data Table Editor. Its often feasible to combine Inline flag with a Hidden flag to hide the Color field itself from the table. See the Row Coloring section below for more information.&lt;/li>&lt;li>If Inline flag is set for a Data Table field, default value of the field will have same format as format of the table to which the field belongs. This effectively enables creation of tables with unlimited nesting using Data Table Editor.&lt;/li>&lt;/ul></help><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field><field advanced="true" description="Encrypted" name="encrypted" type="B"><help>Enables database-level field value encryption.</help><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field><field description="Help" editor="textarea" name="help" nullable="true" type="S"><validators contentType="base64">HFIeW15ccHtDbnRybH1dKl5eRGVzY3JpcHRpb24gbWF5IGNvbnRhaW4gb25seSBwcmludGFibGUgY2hhcmFjdGVycx0=</validators><help>Contents of the pop-up which is displayed to the user when hovering over a field.</help><defaultValue><nullValue/></defaultValue></field><field description="Editor/Viewer" extendableSelectionValues="true" name="editor" nullable="true" type="S"><selectionValues><option description="Default"><nullValue/></option><option description="Date">date</option><option description="Date/Time">dateTime</option><option description="Format Mask">formatString</option><option description="Class Instance">instance</option><option description="Code Editor">code</option><option description="Date Range">dateRange</option><option description="Function Selector">functionselector</option><option description="Sound">sound</option><option description="Text Area">textarea</option><option description="Box">box</option><option description="Reference">reference</option><option description="Evaluation">evaluation</option><option description="Bar">bar</option><option description="Password">password</option><option description="Event Level">eventLevel</option><option description="Context">context</option><option description="HTML">html</option><option description="Hex">hex</option><option description="Text Editor">text</option><option description="Spinner">spinner</option><option description="Image">image</option><option description="Time Period">period</option><option description="Expression">expression</option><option description="IP Address">ip</option><option description="List">list</option><option description="Embedded Text Area">etextarea</option><option description="Foreign Class Instance">foreignInstance</option><option description="Hierarchical List">hierarchicalList</option><option description="Context Mask">contextmask</option><option description="Bytes">bytes</option><option description="Time">time</option><option description="Activator">activator</option><option description="Font">font</option></selectionValues><help>This parameter defines how the field is shown and modified in the user interface.</help><defaultValue><nullValue/></defaultValue></field><field description="Editor Options" name="editorOptions" nullable="true" type="T"><help>Editor/renderer options that allow fine-tuning rendering of field values in the UI.</help><defaultValue><nullValue/></defaultValue></field><field description="Validators" name="validators" nullable="true" type="T"><help>List of validators used to check if value is suitable for the field, as well as validator options. The platform features several pre-configured validators, internally used by the system to verify user input.</help><defaultValue><table><format reorderable="true"><fields><field description="Type" name="validator" nullable="true" type="S"><selectionValues><option description="Default"><nullValue/></option><option description="Regex">R</option><option description="Expression">E</option><option description="ID">I</option><option description="Limits">L</option><option description="Non-Null">N</option></selectionValues><defaultValue><nullValue/></defaultValue></field><field description="Options" name="options" type="S"><defaultValue/></field></fields><bindings><binding><reference>options#options</reference><expression>{validator} == 'E' ? expressionEditorOptions(null) : ""</expression></binding></bindings></format></table></defaultValue></field><field description="Group" name="group" nullable="true" type="S"><help>A human-readable name of a field group. All fields that belong to the same group will appear together within the UI.</help><defaultValue><nullValue/></defaultValue></field></fields><bindings><binding><reference>editorOptions</reference><expression>callFunction("utilities", "editorOptions", {type}, {editor}, {editorOptions})</expression></binding><binding><reference>editor#choices</reference><expression>{utilities:editors('{type}')}</expression></binding></bindings><validators contentType="base64">HEseHRxWHh0=</validators></format></table></defaultValue></field><field description="Reorderable" name="reorderable" type="B"><help>This flag indicates that records in this table may be swapped (re-ordered) during table processing.</help><defaultValue>1</defaultValue></field><field description="Unresizable" name="unresizable" type="B"><help>This flag indicates that users cannot add or remove rows when editing the table.</help><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field><field description="Bindings" name="bindings" type="T"><help>A list of data bindings that define how the values in the table are changed when other table cells, or environment variables, are changed during table processing.</help><defaultValue><table><format reorderable="true"><fields><field description="Target" name="target" type="S"><validators contentType="base64">HEweMSAyMTQ3NDgzNjQ3HQ==</validators><help>The binding's &lt;i>Target&lt;/i> field has the following syntax: &lt;b>variable$field[row]#property&lt;/b>. All elements of the binding target are optional, except for the &lt;b>field&lt;/b>. It indicates the field in the table to which changes should be applied.</help><defaultValue/></field><field description="Expression" editor="expression" name="expression" type="S"><editorOptions contentType="base64"></editorOptions><validators contentType="base64">HEweMSAyMTQ3NDgzNjQ3HQ==</validators><help>The binding expression may contain only standard references. If a reference points to a cell within the table being edited, it will resolve to the value currently contained in the cell (which may be edited by a user, or written by other binding). In all other cases value will be retrieved from the server context, as described in standard references section.</help><defaultValue/></field></fields></format></table></defaultValue></field><field advanced="true" description="Encoded" editor="textarea" name="encoded" readonly="true" type="S"><help>Encoded table format</help><defaultValue/></field><field description="Naming Expression" editor="expression" name="namingExpression" nullable="true" type="S"><editorOptions contentType="base64"></editorOptions><help>An Expression that defines how the table is presented to the users in the interface. It must return a string that will be user as the table's description.</help><defaultValue><nullValue/></defaultValue></field></fields><validators contentType="base64">HEUeZTIxcGJsSmxZMjl5WkhOOUlEdzlJSHR0WVhoU1pXTnZjbVJ6ZlNBL0lHNTFiR3dnT2lBblZHaGxJRzFoZUdsdGRXMGdiblZ0WW1WeUlHOW1JSEpsWTI5eVpITWdZMkZ1Ym05MElHSmxJR3h2ZDJWeUlIUm9ZVzRnZEdobElHMXBibWx0ZFcwbh0=</validators></format><records><record/></records></table></defaultValue></field><field description="Granule Value Expression" editor="expression" extendableSelectionValues="true" name="granuleValueExpression" type="S"><editorOptions contentType="base64"></editorOptions><help>An expression used to evaluate a new aggregated value based on the previous value and the new incoming variable value.</help><defaultValue/></field><field description="Granule Timestamp Expression" editor="expression" extendableSelectionValues="true" name="granuleTimestampExpression" type="S"><editorOptions contentType="base64"></editorOptions><help>An expression used to determine and identify time periods.</help><defaultValue/></field><field description="Granule Expiration Period" editor="period" extendableSelectionValues="true" name="granuleExpirationPeriod" type="L"><help>A period of time that defines how long a granule will be stored.</help><defaultValue>31536000000</defaultValue></field><field advanced="true" description="Granule Timestamp Precision" editor="period" extendableSelectionValues="true" name="granuleTimestampPrecision" type="L"><help>The precision parameter defines a time interval used to locate granules based on a timestamp. Due to rounding errors, a granule's timestamp may differ from the calculated value. Therefore, the granule search engine identifies a granule that lies within an interval around the calculated timestamp. This interval is defined as (timestamp - precision, timestamp + precision).</help><defaultValue>10</defaultValue></field><field description="Inherited From" editor="context" name="inheritedFrom" nullable="true" readonly="true" type="S"><editorOptions contentType="base64"></editorOptions><help>The model that the entity inherits.</help><defaultValue><nullValue/></defaultValue></field></fields><bindings><binding><reference>variable#choices</reference><expression>{.:variablesByMask({.:})}</expression></binding></bindings><validators contentType="base64">HEseHQ==</validators></format></entry><entry><int>13</int><format><fields><field name="variable" type="S"><defaultValue/></field></fields></format></entry></formats></formats></root>